#: ../../../../../../docs/tutorials/async-io.md:8
msgid "沿一次 UART 请求理解借用"
msgstr "Follow a UART request to understand borrowing"

#: ../../../../../../docs/tutorials/async-io.md:10
msgid ""
"先完成[Native 应用](first-native.md)。本教程使用同一份已运行的 `main.c`， "
"沿问候消息检查有限请求的准备、接纳、结清和停止，不建立第二份模拟驱动。"
msgstr ""
"First complete the [Native application](first-native.md). This tutorial uses"
" the same working `main.c` to trace greeting-message preparation, admission,"
" settlement and stop for a finite request. It does not create a second "
"simulated driver."

#: ../../../../../../docs/tutorials/async-io.md:13
msgid "找到真实请求与存储"
msgstr "Locate the real request and storage"

#: ../../../../../../docs/tutorials/async-io.md:15
msgid ""
"打开生成工程的 `main.c`。`s_request` 和 `s_message` 为静态对象， `send_greeting` 使用绝对 "
"deadline 准备请求，经 `nx_uart_port_submit` 提交， 再由同一个执行者调用 `nx_uart_port_service`。"
msgstr ""
"Open the generated project's `main.c`. `s_request` and `s_message` are "
"static objects. `send_greeting` prepares a request with an absolute "
"deadline, submits it through `nx_uart_port_submit`, and has the same "
"executor call `nx_uart_port_service`."

#: ../../../../../../docs/tutorials/async-io.md:19
msgid ""
"准备失败或提交被拒绝时，请求未开始借用。提交成功后，循环持续观察 `NX_REQUEST_SETTLED`，不会在 deadline "
"到达时立即退出并复用存储。 应用随后读取最终结果与已传输数量，只有结清或拒绝后才调用平台停止。"
msgstr ""
"When preparation fails or submission is rejected, the request has not begun "
"a borrow. After successful submission, the loop keeps observing "
"`NX_REQUEST_SETTLED`; it does not immediately exit and reuse storage when "
"the deadline arrives. The application then reads the final result and "
"transferred count, and calls platform stop only after settlement or "
"rejection."

#: ../../../../../../docs/tutorials/async-io.md:23
msgid "执行并检查顺序"
msgstr "Execute and inspect the ordering"

#: ../../../../../../docs/tutorials/async-io.md:25
msgid "设置 `PRODUCT_DIR` 为之前创建的工程路径，再运行："
msgstr "Set `PRODUCT_DIR` to the previously created project path, then run:"

#: ../../../../../../docs/tutorials/async-io.md:32
msgid ""
"`starter_application` 应通过。核对源代码中的顺序：启动 Platform、取得 "
"`NX_UART_REF_CONSOLE`、准备和提交、持续 service、观察结清、读取结果、停止。 factory 获取本身不分配或初始化硬件。"
msgstr ""
"`starter_application` should pass. Check the source ordering: start "
"Platform, acquire `NX_UART_REF_CONSOLE`, prepare and submit, continue "
"service, observe settlement, read the result, then stop. Factory acquisition"
" itself neither allocates nor initializes hardware."

#: ../../../../../../docs/tutorials/async-io.md:36
msgid "把规则带到自己的应用"
msgstr "Apply the rules to your application"

#: ../../../../../../docs/tutorials/async-io.md:38
msgid ""
"换成通知或等待适配时，保留同一个绝对 deadline 和最终请求谓词。通知是提示， 不是完成本身。多个 producer 需要明确 "
"owner；不要阻塞唯一能推进请求的执行者。"
msgstr ""
"When introducing notification or wait adaptation, retain the same absolute "
"deadline and final request predicate. Notification is a hint, not completion"
" itself. Multiple producers require an explicit owner; do not block the only"
" executor able to advance the request."

#: ../../../../../../docs/tutorials/async-io.md:41
msgid ""
"取消、超时和 `QUARANTINED` 不结束借用。失败排空时保留请求、payload 和有关 控制／观察者状态，按实际 owner "
"继续处理。并非所有等待都能证明有限停机。"
msgstr ""
"Cancellation, timeout and `QUARANTINED` do not end a borrow. If drain fails,"
" retain the request, payload and relevant control/observer state, and "
"continue handling them under the actual owner. Not every wait can establish "
"bounded shutdown."

#: ../../../../../../docs/tutorials/async-io.md:44
msgid ""
"当前模式与限制见[支持参考](../reference/platforms/support.md)，完整规则见 [I/O "
"执行](../guides/io-execution.md)和[所有权](../explanation/ownership.md)。 "
"实现维护者可进一步查看 `tests/behavior/io/native_async_test.cpp` 的拒绝、取消和 结清回归；这些回归不替代真实"
" DMA／线路时序测量。"
msgstr ""
"See the [support reference](../reference/platforms/support.md) for current "
"modes and limitations, and [I/O execution](../guides/io-execution.md) and "
"[ownership](../explanation/ownership.md) for complete rules. Implementation "
"maintainers may inspect rejection, cancellation and settlement regressions "
"in `tests/behavior/io/native_async_test.cpp`. Those regressions do not "
"replace real DMA/wire timing measurements."
